# fetch (github.com/areofyl/fetch): the fastfetch logo spun in 3D.
# Without this dir fetch asks fastfetch for the logo, and config.jsonc there
# maps logo colour 1 to the default foreground (meant for the flat logo), so
# the 3D one came out white. logo.txt is the same Max Theorum art without the
# $1 placeholders; a logo of its own gets two colours by surface. The value
# lands verbatim in "ESC[1;<value>m", so a name (red ... white), an SGR number
# (94) or a truecolor triple (38;2;R;G;B) all work. Faces in Catppuccin Mocha
# text (the flat logo's colour); sides in overlay2, a darker step of the same
# grey, since the outline has so few side cells that a second hue reads as
# stray pixels.
logo_inner=38;2;205;214;244
logo_outer=38;2;147;153;178
# Fields, in order: once this file exists only the listed ones show, and the
# logo is drawn in the rows the info block takes, so an empty list also
# squeezes the logo to two rows. Same modules as fastfetch's config.jsonc.
uptime
os
kernel
packages
wm
terminal
shell
cpu
memory
disk
battery
colors
